{"level":"intermediate","title":"How it works","questions":[{"id":"L3-001","level":"intermediate","q":"What is Script in Bitcoin?","choices":["a mining program","Bitcoin's spending-condition language","a wallet app","a block format"],"answer":1,"source":"bitcoin.org developer docs, transactions"},{"id":"L3-002","level":"intermediate","q":"What is P2PKH?","choices":["pay to public key hash: 1... addresses","pay to script: 3... addresses","a SegWit address","a Lightning invoice"],"answer":0,"source":"bitcoin.org developer docs, transactions"},{"id":"L3-003","level":"intermediate","q":"What is P2SH?","choices":["a bech32 address","a Taproot address","a private key","pay to script hash: 3... addresses"],"answer":3,"source":"BIP-16"},{"id":"L3-004","level":"intermediate","q":"What is P2WPKH?","choices":["a 1... address","a 3... address","a SegWit bc1q... address","a Lightning invoice"],"answer":2,"source":"BIP-141, BIP-173"},{"id":"L3-005","level":"intermediate","q":"What is P2TR?","choices":["a 1... address","a Taproot bc1p... address","a 3... address","an xpub"],"answer":1,"source":"BIP-341, BIP-350"},{"id":"L3-006","level":"intermediate","q":"What is the witness in SegWit?","choices":["signature data kept aside from the tx hash","a miner's signature","a wallet backup","a block header"],"answer":0,"source":"BIP-141"},{"id":"L3-007","level":"intermediate","q":"What is transaction malleability?","choices":["melting coins","losing keys","changing a tx id without changing its spends","forging signatures"],"answer":2,"source":"BIP-141"},{"id":"L3-008","level":"intermediate","q":"What is OP_RETURN?","choices":["a refund code","an opcode storing small data in a transaction","a miner vote","a wallet reset"],"answer":1,"source":"bitcoin.org developer docs, transactions"},{"id":"L3-009","level":"intermediate","q":"What does nLockTime do?","choices":["a wallet lock","a password timer","a mining delay","a transaction valid only after a time or height"],"answer":3,"source":"bitcoin